{{- /*
  pr_description.user: the Publish-phase prompt for generating a PR
  title + body from structured signals (feature context, roadmap, commit
  bodies, diff stat). The raw line-level diff is intentionally NOT
  injected — commit messages + stats are sufficient for description and
  fit comfortably inside CLI prompt budgets even on very large features.

  Output format is rigid: TITLE: + BODY: markers so ParsePRDescription
  can split deterministically.
*/ -}}
{{- define "pr_description.user" -}}
# Generate PR Description

{{ if or .FeatureName .FeatureDescription }}## Feature

{{ if .FeatureName }}Name: {{ .FeatureName }}

{{ end }}{{ if .FeatureDescription }}{{ .FeatureDescription }}

{{ end }}{{ end }}{{ if .Roadmap }}## Roadmap / Plan

{{ .Roadmap }}

{{ end }}{{ if .CommitBodies }}## Commit Messages

```
{{ .CommitBodies }}
```

{{ end }}{{ if .DiffStat }}## Changes (file stats)

```
{{ .DiffStat }}
```

{{ end }}## Instructions

Generate a pull request description using the feature, roadmap, commit messages,
and file-level change stats above. The raw line-level diff is intentionally not
included — rely on the commit messages and stats to describe the change.

Produce:
1. A concise title (under 70 characters) that captures the feature intent
2. A Summary section with 1-3 bullets on what changed and why
3. A Test plan section

Output format (exactly):
TITLE: <title>
BODY:
<body in markdown>
{{ end -}}
